  "type": "physicalTech",
  "system": {
    "description": "<p>This loose poncho contains a network of sensors that perceive wavelengths from microwave to ultra-violet. A similar network of miniature emitters precisely replicate the information its sensors receive, making you seem transparent to those wavelengths while covered by the cloak. Apply a +10 modifier to Infiltrate Tests, +30 if stationary and completely covered. Chameleon cloaks are not effective against radar, x-ray, or gamma-ray sensors. They do hide you from thermal infrared, however, by absorbing body heat into a heat sink. The cloak can only absorb body heat for one hour before it must emit this heat. Heat emission also requires one hour, during which time you are easily visible in the thermal infrared spectrum.</p>",
    "reference": "Eclipse Phase Second Edition p. 338",
